        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=Format this trip into a beautiful HTML email:\n\nRecipient: {{ $json.body.email }}\nMood: {{ $json.body.moodEmoji }} {{ $json.body.moodName }}\n\nTrip Title: {{ $json.body.itinerary.title }}\nPlace: {{ $json.body.itinerary.place }}\nDates: {{ $json.body.itinerary.range }}\nSummary: {{ $json.body.itinerary.summary }}\n\nStats: {{ JSON.stringify($json.body.itinerary.stats) }}\n\nDay-by-day itinerary: {{ JSON.stringify($json.body.itinerary.days) }}\n\nTips: {{ JSON.stringify($json.body.itinerary.tips) }}\n\nPacking list: {{ JSON.stringify($json.body.itinerary.packing) }}\n\nPreferences: {{ $json.body.preferences.budget }} budget, {{ $json.body.preferences.scope }}, {{ $json.body.preferences.length }} trip, {{ $json.body.preferences.company }}\n",
        "options": {
          "systemMessage": "You are an email designer for WanderMood, a mood-based travel app. \nYou receive trip itinerary data and format it into a beautiful, warm HTML email.\n\nRules:\n- Use inline CSS only (email clients don't support <style> tags)\n- Keep the design warm, elegant, earthy tones (backgrounds: #F9F7F4, text: #2C2520, accent: #8B7355)\n- Use Georgia/serif for headings, system sans-serif for body\n- Include: mood emoji + name, trip title, place, date range, summary, stats, day-by-day schedule, tips, and packing list\n- Make it mobile-friendly (max-width: 600px, centered)\n- Add a WanderMood header and footer\n- Output ONLY the raw HTML — no markdown fences, no explanation\n"
        }
      },
